{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# J6 — Data Center transport on `pycontribs/jira`, behind an opt-in extra\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nThe DC backend needs a transport satisfying rebar's `TicketTransport` role plus `SupportsLinks`,\n`SupportsComments`, and `SupportsAbsenceProbe` (`_backend.py:80-282`). The Cloud transport is an ACLI subprocess\n(`adapters/jira/acli_subprocess.py:31` shells out to the `acli` binary), which is Cloud-shaped and must not be\ndisturbed. PR #120 hand-rolled a stdlib `urllib` REST v2 client for DC.\n\n## Approach\n\nBuild the DC transport on **`pycontribs/jira`**, the maintained Python client that already handles Server/DC\nversus Cloud differences, PAT bearer auth, pagination, and payload quirks that a hand-rolled client would\nrediscover. It is confined to an opt-in `[jira-datacenter]` extra and imported **lazily inside the functions\nthat need it**, so the engine's `dependencies = []` contract holds and `import rebar` stays dependency-free; a\nmissing extra raises a clear install-naming error, mirroring `runner._import_pydantic_ai`.\n\nAuth is a Personal Access Token read env-only from `JIRA_PAT` (DC PATs, Jira 8.14+), passed as\n`token_auth`; `url` and `project` come from the typed config so a `[tool.rebar.jira]` value is honored. A\nmalformed config **fails loudly** rather than degrading to env-only — PR #120 swallowed `ConfigError`, which is\nagainst rebar's fail-loud posture.\n\nThe library's object model is unwrapped at this boundary: every method returns the **raw payload shapes**\nrebar's existing mappers already consume (`{\"key\": …, \"fields\": {…}}`), so nothing downstream learns about\n`jira.Issue`. Retry, timeout, and error typing are mapped onto rebar's existing transport contract — transient\nconnectivity faults retried with the same 2s/5s backoff as\n`adapters/jira/acli_rest._rest_urlopen_with_retry`, HTTP errors never retried, and assignee failures raised as\n`BackendAssigneeNotFoundError` (`_backend.py:48`).\n\nThis story also supplies the `NameIdentity` resolver's user-search lookup [rebar:0a94-e104-7304-4d85].\n\n**Alternative rejected: a hand-rolled stdlib client (PR #120).** Competent, but it re-owns Jira REST semantics\nthat a widely-used library has already hardened, and confining the dependency to an extra means non-DC users\npay nothing for it.\n\n**Alternative rejected: reusing the ACLI transport for DC.** ACLI is the Cloud-validated path; pointing it at\nDC would risk the one transport we have live confidence in, which this epic explicitly must not do.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/transport.py` (new).\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/settings.py` (new) — `JIRA_URL`/`JIRA_PROJECT`\n  from typed config, env-only `JIRA_PAT`, fail-loud on `ConfigError`.\n- `pyproject.toml` — `[jira-datacenter]` extra.\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_jira_dc_transport.py` (new); `tests/live_jira_dc/test_transport.py` (new).\n\n## Testing\n\nTwo tiers. A stateful fake for fast unit coverage of shape mapping, and the J5 harness [rebar:c97f-90ae-4976-47c7] as the\nreal oracle — the test-design standard's \"stateful verified fake plus a live canary where justified\", and DC\nsemantics are exactly where a fake's assumptions are most likely to be wrong.\n\n- unit (fake library client): each `TicketTransport` method returns rebar's raw payload shape, not a\n  `jira.Issue`; `JIRA_PAT` is sent as bearer token auth; a missing `[jira-datacenter]` extra raises naming the\n  install command; a malformed config raises rather than degrading.\n- unit failure paths: an HTTP error is NOT retried (call count is exactly 1) while a connection timeout IS\n  retried with the documented backoff; an unknown assignee raises `BackendAssigneeNotFoundError`.\n- live (J5 harness): create → read → update → transition-by-name → comment → link → probe a real issue and\n  assert each observable postcondition on the server, including that a transition to a name the workflow does\n  not offer raises rather than silently no-oping.\n- live edge: the absence probe returns the classifier's not-found state for a deleted issue, and a distinct\n  state for one that merely lost permission.\n- collateral invariant: no Cloud test changes and `adapters/jira/acli*.py` are untouched.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] every `TicketTransport`, `SupportsLinks`, `SupportsComments`, and `SupportsAbsenceProbe` method has a\n      passing live test against the J5 harness, output summarized in a ticket comment\n- [ ] a test asserts an HTTP error is attempted exactly once and a timeout is retried per the documented backoff\n- [ ] `pip install nava-rebar` then `pip show jira` reports not-installed, and `import rebar` succeeds\n- [ ] importing the DC transport without the extra raises an error naming `pip install nava-rebar[jira-datacenter]`\n- [ ] a malformed `[tool.rebar.jira]` config raises `ConfigError` rather than falling back to env-only\n- [ ] `git diff --stat` shows no change under `adapters/jira/acli*`"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785010376009577001,"uuid":"d527548c-a51f-4579-8be6-81e1d1cc92e1"}